{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"655080c7ef113e82","type":"text","text":"[[Yormindar.canvas]]\n#Volstarian_Dynasty ","x":-780,"y":-740,"width":250,"height":70},
		{"id":"91359cbd024de1b7","type":"text","text":"Web of the Spider Queen:\n\nDeep in the depths of the Residuum mines lies the Web of the Spider Queen, a den of drows who are all enslaved and mind controlled by Loth and lead by one given the title of Lothina.\n","x":-800,"y":-580,"width":560,"height":160},
		{"id":"1e53a8e12db5c48b","type":"text","text":"Halls of silk:\n\nThe halls of silk are a series of tunnels that lead into the den its self. There are usually phase spiders driders and other disgusting creatures down here however at the time of the parties first arrival all of the creatures are either dead or warded off. There are directions in the form of red markings on the cave walls that lead toward the den\n\n","x":-800,"y":-300,"width":517,"height":213},
		{"id":"cd66f4eeacd66da8","type":"text","text":"The Web: \n\nThe web its self is a gargantuan labyrinth with twisting corridors however the path through the halls from the emberhold lead directly to the bottom floor which is still a maze in its self.\n\nThe bottom floor is littered with traps and usually heavily guarded by Loth sworn Drow however at the time of the parties first arrival it will have no life but still be riddled with traps. This entire place is covered in spider webs in is faintly illuminated by purple torches that flicker.\n\nThe walls are made of a dark black stone brick same on the floor and ceiling the halls themselves are barren but there are a few places of interest.\n","x":-609,"y":100,"width":652,"height":340},
		{"id":"49437b888e04fd68","type":"text","text":"The cells:\n\nLocated within the web there is a prison where Xandars family is currently being held and the entire room is littered with traps but again there are no gaurds.\n\nThe prison chambers can be described via the map made.\n\n","x":-40,"y":620,"width":583,"height":213},
		{"id":"a19b30a8d9ad0cdd","type":"text","text":"The Queens Lair:\n\nThe Queens Lair is deep at the very back of the bottom floor of the Labyrinth opposite to the prison cells.\n\nThis Lair it lined with silver and platinum walls and at the far end is a throne made of the corpse of a spider. In the center of the lair there is a statue of the spider queen her self and off to the far left a locked vault. Sitting on the throne at all times is Lolthina who at the time of the parties first arrival is actually on a leash being held by a man sitting in the throne with a black hood. The walls are lined with the commandments of the spider Queen and a depiction of her inflicting her will among the world.\n\n","x":-1000,"y":640,"width":700,"height":280},
		{"id":"f0102e3f14c001ab","type":"text","text":"The Vault:\n\nTo get into the vault you need the key or to pass a DC 30 sleight of hand check. \n\nThe vault is a cube shaped chamber and is elegant and has a posh touch to it which is unsettling given the surrounding area. The vault walls are lined with platinum and silver and on the ceiling in the center of the room there is a drawing in the marble stone of a Drow woman sitting on the body of a spider.\n\nLoot within the vault:\n\nIoun stone, Leadership \nCloak of Arachnida\nCarpet of Flying, 4 ft. × 6 ft.\n\n400 platinum \n2000 gold\n489 silver\n500 copper\n\n","x":-987,"y":1040,"width":654,"height":440},
		{"id":"1d83134202d1428c","type":"text","text":"The lair walls:\n\nThe walls show a drow woman with 8 eyes gazing at the world trying to grasp it with her hands as her hands approach webs begin to attach to Villatos right as a heart shaped object appears in front of her unleashing a ravaging blast of energy warding off the spider queen\n","x":-40,"y":920,"width":557,"height":172},
		{"id":"80905272da44bd68","type":"file","file":"Volstarian Dynasty/Forest of Milora/Yormindar/Images/Pasted image 20260915191742.png","x":-120,"y":1220,"width":559,"height":440},
		{"id":"22087e5b8ea987bd","type":"file","file":"Volstarian Dynasty/Forest of Milora/Yormindar/Images/Pasted image 20260915191752.png","x":-220,"y":1700,"width":879,"height":450},
		{"id":"a61a8528faf633f2","type":"file","file":"Volstarian Dynasty/Forest of Milora/Yormindar/Images/Pasted image 20260915191801.png","x":-220,"y":2200,"width":768,"height":797}
	],
